<article class="env-definition" id="03CT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03CT">Definition <span data-tag="03CT">18.9.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a presheaf of rings on $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>presheaf of $\mathcal{O}$-modules</em> is given by an abelian presheaf $\mathcal{F}$ together with a map of presheaves of sets 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O} \times \mathcal{F} \longrightarrow \mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
<p>
 such that for every object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ the map $\mathcal{O}(U) \times \mathcal{F}(U) \to \mathcal{F}(U)$ defines the structure of an $\mathcal{O}(U)$-module structure on the abelian group $\mathcal{F}(U)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ of presheaves of $\mathcal{O}$-modules</em> is a morphism of abelian presheaves $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ such that the diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{O} \times \mathcal{F} \ar[r] \ar[d]_{\text{id} \times \varphi } &  \mathcal{F} \ar[d]^{\varphi } \\  \mathcal{O} \times \mathcal{G} \ar[r] &  \mathcal{G} }  \]
</div>
<p>
 commutes. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The set of $\mathcal{O}$-module morphisms as above is denoted $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {O}(\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{G})$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The category of presheaves of $\mathcal{O}$-modules is denoted $\textit{PMod}(\mathcal{O})$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>